Error [E2710]: built-in codec derive generated invalid Jet for `Order`
  --> tests/ui/serde_flatten_not_struct.jet:3:2
    |
  3 | #Codable
    |  ^^^^^^^
 Why: generated source did not pass the ordinary lexer and parser: expected `::` or `:=` in a binding, found `:` at Some(Span { start: 53, end: 54 }); generated source:
impl Order.Encode {
fn encode(self) -> DataTree {
out: [String: DataTree] := []
nested :: self.count.encode()
if nested == .Object(entries) { loop key, value; entries { out[key] = value } }
return DataTree.Object(out)
}
}
impl Order.Decode {
fn decode(tree: DataTree) -> Order ? DecodeError {
return Ok(Order.{
count: tree.decode<Int>()?,
})
}
}

 Fix: report this compiler bug; built-in derives must emit valid ordinary Jet

Error [E2408]: `#[Flatten]` on `count` needs a struct-typed field
  --> tests/ui/serde_flatten_not_struct.jet:5:16
    |
  5 |     #[Flatten] count: Int
    |                ^^^^^
 Why: flatten splices another struct's keys into this object, so the field must be a `#[Codable]` struct — not a primitive, list, or map
 Fix: give `count` a `#[Codable]` struct type, or drop `#[Flatten]`
